// Web-site    : http://www.rdctools.com
// Created     : 2026-10-14
//
// Description : FlexTron (FT) subclass of cWebMenuItem: an item of a dialog's action menu (cFTActionBarHost),
//               whose work runs after the web click has returned (OnItemClick), as a cFTWebButton's does.
//
// This code is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY;
// without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
//****************************************************************************
Use cWebMenuItem.pkg
Use cFTClickRelay.pkg           // the click relay - OnItemClick runs after the web event has returned

/* AN ITEM OF A DIALOG'S ACTION MENU (Nils 2026-10-14: a dialog's actions in a menu at its top right, as a web view
   has them - the oActionGroup of DataFlex's FlexTron sample ZoomInventory.wo). A dialog puts a cWebMenuGroup in
   its cFTActionBarHost and its items in the group; the host's action bar shows them as FT buttons.

   THE CLICK'S WORK WAITS FOR THE CLICK TO END (cFTClickRelay.pkg): a Yes/No box, a data dictionary's error
   box or a Close_Panel from inside the web event faults (4410). So OnClick only hands the item to the relay, and
   one tick later OnItemClick runs - put an item's work there.

   IN THE BAR ONLY: peActionDisplay is adActionBar. An item that is in the menu too (adBoth, the framework's
   default) or only there (adMenu) puts a More button on the bar, whose list opens below it - and a host only as
   tall as the bar cuts that list off.

   ITS GLYPH is a class in psCSSClass, as a cFTWebButton's is: "ftg-save" (ftglyphs.css draws it in front of
   the caption). An item without one shows its caption only. */
{ DesignerJSClass=df.WebMenuItem }
{ OverrideProperty=peActionDisplay InitialValue=adActionBar }
Class cFTWebMenuItem is a cWebMenuItem

    Procedure Construct_Object
        Forward Send Construct_Object
        Set peActionDisplay to adActionBar
    End_Procedure

    /* The framework's click, inside the WebView2 event. It only hands the item to the relay, so put an item's
       work in OnItemClick. An object that overrides OnClick itself runs its code inside the click - Forward
       it, or OnItemClick never runs. */
    Procedure OnClick
        Send Relay of (FTClickRelay()) Self
    End_Procedure

    // The relay's tick, after the web event has returned - the relay sends a button's message.
    Procedure OnButtonClick
        Send OnItemClick
    End_Procedure

    // The item's work: a request to a host, a box, Close_Panel.
    { MethodType=Event }
    Procedure OnItemClick
    End_Procedure

    // The object the item acts on: the grid, field or data-aware host the focus came from before the menu. The
    // menu's host (cFTActionBarHost) remembers it; the group between them passes the question on.
    Function ActionTarget Returns Handle
        Handle hoTarget
        Delegate Get ActionTarget to hoTarget
        Function_Return hoTarget
    End_Function

End_Class
